course: dictionary
lesson: 91
title: Adapt: changing to fit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To adapt is to change so that you fit a new place or situation better. «Plants and animals are adapted to their climate.» Adapted means changed to fit the weather and the place where they live.
explain: Look at the words around the word. «Muscle soreness a day or two after unusual exercise is normal as muscles adapt, and gentle movement helps.» Muscles change as you use them, so adapt means change to cope. Try your meaning in the sentence: "as muscles change to cope" still makes sense.
explain: Adapt can also mean changing something so it can be used in a new way, or changing a book into a film or play. The word is the same, but the context shows which meaning is right.
fact: Adapt means to change so that you fit a new place or situation better.
fact: Animals and plants have features that help them survive where they live, such as camels for deserts and polar bears for the cold.
fact: Living things adapt over very long times.
fact: «Adapted» means changed to fit, and it is the past form of adapt.
fact: A story can be «adapted from a book» when it is changed into a film or play.
exercise: «Plants and animals are adapted to their climate.» What does adapted mean here? | Afraid of the cold | *Changed to fit their weather and home | Measured carefully | Sold in shops
exercise: Which animal shows an adaptation to the cold? | *A polar bear | A goldfish | A camel
exercise: «The film was adapted from a book.» What does adapted mean here? | Thrown away | *Changed into a film from a book | Read aloud slowly | Printed on paper
test: Ahmed moves to a new school and soon adapts. What does adapts mean? | Leaves school for good | *Changes to fit the new school | Stays exactly the same | Forgets his name
test: In «muscles adapt», which word means the same as adapt? | Grow loud | Freeze | Stop | *Adjust
exam: Which sentence uses adapt to mean changed so something can be used in a new way? | The chef adapts the sky to be blue | *The chef adapts the old recipe so it works in a new oven | The chef adapts a sandwich by eating it | The chef adapts to sleep all day
